WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.468
-Our first guest tonight
is a very

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:05.104
talented actor you know
from movies such as "Whiplash,"

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.940
the "Divergent" franchise,
and "Top Gun: Maverick."

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.310
You can see him in the limited
series "The Offer,"

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.011
which is streaming now
on Paramount+

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.747
and also stars in "Spiderhead,"

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.550
which begins streaming
on Netflix June 17th.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.617
Let's take a look.

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:21.087
-Mark, I mean, look, man,

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.689
I've been on some, some
crazy-ass project teams, right?

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.393
But this one --
this one doesn't feel right.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:30.296
-Jeff, you know, I sympathize,
but only to a point.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.799
Listen, I got to take off my
friendship hat for a second

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.268
and remind you your presence
in this facility,

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.671
while technically a punishment,
is a privilege, is it not?

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.706
You applied for it.
You were approved for it.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:43.108
You could just as easily be
at state, with the general pop,

00:00:43.108 --> 00:00:44.711
then you really would be
playing pitch and catch --

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.612
in your case, catch --
with the likes of Rogan.

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.848
You don't even want to know
what he did in his last prison.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.917
-Please welcome back to the show
Miles Teller, everybody.

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:54.787
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:54.787 --> 00:01:03.362 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.698 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.266
Welcome back to the show, Miles.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.268
I'm so happy you're here.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:11.437
-That's how we do it.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:14.840
-You have so many,
so many projects to talk about,

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.477
but I want to start --
you had a real honor.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:20.312
You grew up in South Jersey
and you got to throw out

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.281
a first pitch
at a Phillies game.

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:23.515
Were you nervous?

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.218
-I was -- I was pretty nervous.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.486
I tried to cancel it
the last minute.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:28.721
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.
-Because I was like,

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.323
"I've done it before."
It just really adds

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.424
like another layer of stress
to the day

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:34.093
because you're doing interviews
and you're --

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:36.128
-Absolutely.
I would say to the week.

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:39.431
I did it exactly one time and I
would never, ever do it again.

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:41.401
[ Laughter ]
-So this was my second time,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:45.071
but I threw from the rubber,
which, that's a big thing.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.739
-The first time,
did you do front grass?

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:47.673
-No, I did the rubber
both times.

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:48.807
-The rubber's a big deal,

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:50.209
to go from the rubber.

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:51.678
-And the photo they get

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.680
[ Cheering and applause ]
is always like --

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.381
no, you don't have
[indistinct] neck.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.082
[ Laughter ]
It's just always --

00:01:57.082 --> 00:01:59.318
I always think of like
Judd, you know, Apatow's photo

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.754
and just the amount of like --
because you're so nervous

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.824
and you're trying so hard
to kind of aim the ball.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.959
It's not very flattering, dude.
-It's a face you very rarely

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:08.794
see actual pitchers have.
-Yeah.

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:11.697
[ Laughter ]
-I want to stress mine is worse

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:13.365
than this, so I'm not --
I'm not judging.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.167
-I noticed you didn't bring
your photo.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.102
-No, I didn't.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.270
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.705
Them's the rules.
-It's your show, Seth.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.240
-When you get to host,
you don't bring the photos.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.275
-Just happy to be here.
-I'll tell you
what I didn't get.

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:25.444
So, was the Bobblehead
given out at the game
you threw out the pitch?

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:27.547
-It was, yeah.
-Now, that's pretty cool,
right here.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.049 line:0%
You got a "Top Gun" Bobblehead.
-That's a much better face.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:30.883 line:0%
[ Cheering, ohs, and applause ]

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:31.817 line:0%
I mean, just the --

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:34.119 line:0%
just the co-branding.

00:02:34.119 --> 00:02:35.888 line:0%
-I know.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.790 line:0%
I know.
That was -- That was pretty --

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.126 line:0%
That was pretty sweet.
Like as a diehard baseball fan

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:44.931
and kind of that little bit
of crossover was very nice.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.733
Like there's some real nice
details to it.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.634
And congrats on this movie,

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.370
which, you know, so, "Top Gun,"
you finished in 2019

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.272
and, you know, I think it's been
well-reported on

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:55.107
that it was -- it was delayed
until people could go back

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:56.576
and see it in theaters.
-Yeah.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.411
Did it feel great knowing you
had this really exciting thing

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:00.880
that people were eventually
going to see

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.881
or were you just like
chomping at the bit,

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:04.083
desperate for people to see it?

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.985
-I'd done a good amount
of movies beforehand

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.320
and so I didn't --
I didn't feel like

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.823
I needed this movie
to ensure future work.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.325
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.926
But some of the actors in it,

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:16.362
you know, this was such
a big showcase for them

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.663
and, if anything,

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.433
I really was just bummed
for the -- for the fans

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:24.003
because the fans, we found,
are just like insane.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.238
[ Cheering and applause ]
They're so ravenous
and they've been waiting.

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:29.241
Okay, we got some here.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.544
I knew I could feel the
"Top Gun" fans in the audience.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.546
[ Laughter ]
Warmed up a little bit.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.881
But no, so, really, I was just,
I was bummed for the fans

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:37.283
and I couldn't wait for them
to see it

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.952
because I knew, as you've --
you know, you've seen the movie.

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:42.521
It's just been like --
It's been a rocket, so.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:45.291
[ Cheering and applause ]
-You were actually --

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.259
Again, much has been written
about the fact

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:48.994
that you guys were actually --
I had Jon Hamm here.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:50.463
He did not go up in the planes.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.264
He did nothing.
-I know.

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:54.467
-But you were in these planes.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.936
-And was it awful?

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.437
[ Laughter ]
-It was --

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:01.740
I'm not signing up to do it --
Even like I was at the Indy 500

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.577
and, you know, the Thunderbirds,
who are amazing,

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.612
they fly in formation --

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.847
everybody wants
to take me up now and fly

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:10.483
and I just --
I'm like, "It's --"

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.751
They go, "We can take you up
when you're in Las Vegas,"

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:15.421
and I go, "Honestly, there's not
a place I'd want to go less

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.456
[ Laughter ]
than like -- Not Las Vegas,

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:20.793
but I'm saying I would not want
to go up in your jet

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:23.930
and fly in formation
after being in Las Vegas,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.831
is what I'm saying.
-That's a good point, right.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:26.865
You stay out late.
You're like,

00:04:26.865 --> 00:04:28.534
"What am I doing this morning?
Oh, no!"

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.568
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:32.605
"Oh, I forgot I said yes
to that thing.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.707
That's not going to be good."
-Did you think

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:35.741
you could fly a plane now,

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:36.842
after being up there
with pilots?

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:38.044
I know you weren't doing
the actual flying.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.645
-It depends on who's
in the plane...

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:40.847
-Yeah, that's a good point,
right.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.815
-...you know?
Like if it's by myself

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.817
and I had to, I'll bet on it,

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:48.320
but if I had to like,
if it was my wife or, you know,

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.589
my dog or my mom or something...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:52.291
I would -- I don't --

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.293
yeah, I wouldn't want that
responsibility, Seth.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:55.962
-I don't think I would be able
to do it

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.497
with my mom in the plane,
just because I think she'd have

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.999
a lot of like, "No, no, no!"

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.333
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:02.969
It's like, "I did it in a movie,
Mom, relax."

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:05.337
-You just relax!
"You're going too fast!"

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:07.640
[ Laughter ]
-Fanboy, fanboy.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.075
-What was your --
Didn't you have like a --

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.644
like an allergic reaction
to a plane or something?

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.778
What was the story?
-Yeah, I told you that

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:15.147
in private, Seth.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:18.184
No, I thought that's what
we were -- Yeah, I --

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:21.119
Yeah, I landed.
We got done.

00:05:21.119 --> 00:05:22.588
They're called a sortie,
basically,

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.189
when you go up
and you do some stuff.

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:26.526
And so we landed.
I'm just like, "Man,

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.460
I'm not feeling too good,"
and I was like getting --

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.497
I was really hot and I just
started itching like crazy,

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.400
so I get out of the jet
and I'm just covered in hives,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.804
like head to toe.
Instantly, I go to a doctor.

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:41.039
I do like a blood analysis,
this, that, whatever.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:42.709
I'm in an oatmeal bath at night.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:45.144
Like I have sensitive skin,
anyway,

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.044
[ Laughter ]
truth be told,

00:05:46.044 --> 00:05:47.680
like Irish/Scottish skin.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.650
[ Laughter ]
No dyes, no nothing.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.785
-Ideally, no sun.
-Nothing.

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.820
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.388
-I can get some sun.
-You can get a little sun, yeah.

00:05:56.388 --> 00:05:58.023
[ Laughter ]
-It's "Top Gun," baby.

00:05:58.023 --> 00:06:00.092
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:02.328
Whoo! So, anyway, so, like
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:03.829
I go to the doctor

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:06.198
and my bloodwork comes back
and I have

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:09.402
flame-retardant pesticides
and jet fuel in my blood.

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:10.936
[ Ohs ]
-Oh, my God.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:12.537
-That's what I thought,
but then I thought,

00:06:12.537 --> 00:06:14.373
[ Laughter ]
"Wait a second.
This is actually kind of cool."

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:16.976
[ Laughter ]
So I go to set the next day

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.611
and Tom's like,
"So how did it go, Miles?

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:22.314
What did they find?"
I was like, "Well, Tom,
it turns out

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:24.016
I have jet fuel in my blood."

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.484
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.687
And without even skipping
a beat, Tom just goes,

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.755
"Yeah, I was born with it, kid."

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:31.223
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:33.092
-There's your Top Gun.
-Yeah.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:37.162
So that was like a very Tom
moment for me.

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:39.731
-Now, your director also
directed "Spiderhead," correct?

00:06:39.731 --> 00:06:42.134
-Yeah, Joseph Kosinski.
-Which is really cool.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:43.536
Obviously did a great job
with that.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:45.505
This is a -- a very different
kind of film.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:48.607
This is based
on George Saunders' short story,

00:06:48.607 --> 00:06:50.008
one I love a great deal.

00:06:50.008 --> 00:06:52.444
-Yeah, so it's based on the
George Saunders short story

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:55.247
in The New Yorker,
"Escape from Spiderhead."

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:56.982
It's myself.
It's Chris Hemsworth.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:59.952
It's Jurnee Smollett.
Joseph Kosinski directing it

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:03.455
and we filmed it during COVID
in Australia.

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.224
The movie, basically, is

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:08.160
Chris Hemsworth's character
runs a facility.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.830
He's kind of half hippie,
half mad scientist.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:15.167
All the inmates in this facility
voluntarily go there,

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:17.536
instead of kind of going
and serving prison time.

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:19.705
They're all criminals.
And we are under

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.873
the experimentation
of Chris Hemsworth

00:07:21.873 --> 00:07:24.343
and -- and a lot
of different drugs

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:26.979
[ Laughter ]
and some are fun,

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.814
some are -- some are terrifying.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:28.814 --> 00:07:30.482
-And so that's kind of
the premise.

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:32.318
How we -- How we deal
with inmates, too,

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:33.619
and how we should deal
with criminals

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.687
and, if it's really
about reformation,

00:07:35.687 --> 00:07:37.056
then why are we putting them
in a prison system

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:39.258
where they don't --
I don't think they come

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:41.460
out of prison being,
you know, model citizens.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.863
I don't think that's really
what our prison system is doing.

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:45.330
So, there's some
larger themes there.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:48.634
But, yeah, I mean, that's
kind of the nuts and bolts.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.537
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah. It's really cool.

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:53.572
And, like we said,
with the introduction,

00:07:53.572 --> 00:07:55.040
you've been so busy.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.942
"The Offer,"
I'm enjoying a great deal.

00:07:56.942 --> 00:07:58.177
-Whoo!
-Thank you.
-This is about the making

00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:00.746
of "The Godfather"
and it's incredible,

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:02.214
this movie I've seen
so many times,

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:06.118
how little I knew about all the
hurdles leading up to making it.

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.453
It must've been such
a cool project.

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:10.922
Going into it,
did you know this backstory?

00:08:10.922 --> 00:08:13.525
-Not really. I think I knew
a little bit about

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:17.162
how they didn't want Al Pacino,
but I didn't know

00:08:17.162 --> 00:08:18.597
they didn't want
Francis Ford Coppola.

00:08:18.597 --> 00:08:20.866
They didn't want Marlon Brando.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:23.568
-Studio executives
sometimes nail it, yeah.

00:08:23.568 --> 00:08:26.839
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:29.642
-And so, it was just, yeah,
there were a lot of obstacles,

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:32.277
but the biggest one
that I realized was the mob.

00:08:32.277 --> 00:08:34.614
I mean, the Mafia,
to shoot in New York,

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:36.749
they really did control
all the Teamsters.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.850
They were the Teamsters
in New York, so,

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.353
they talk about they would go
into a building

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:42.721
like in Little Italy
or whatever it is.

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:44.923
They'd come out and all
their equipment would be gone.

00:08:44.923 --> 00:08:46.058
So you really did kind of have

00:08:46.058 --> 00:08:47.993
to have like a handshake
with the Mafia

00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:50.295
because they didn't want
"The Godfather" to be made

00:08:50.295 --> 00:08:52.999
because they said the Mafia
is a word that's, you know,

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:56.669
keeping Italian American
immigrants down

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.771
"and this movie is only going
to make us look like savages.

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:02.408
We're not. We're proud people,"
and et cetera, et cetera.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:03.876
So, also, in the movie,

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:06.946
the word Mafia doesn't exist
one time.

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:10.382
They took that out of the script
and that was a big a big reason

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:11.616
why they were able
to get it made, actually.

00:09:11.616 --> 00:09:13.418
-That's incredible
because you definitely knew

00:09:13.418 --> 00:09:15.187
it was about the Mafia,
even without the word in there.

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:16.222
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.222 --> 00:09:18.457
-I know.
-Yeah. They were like,

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:20.125
[ Italian accent ] Don't worry.
I took care of it.

00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:23.462
Nobody's going to know."
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:24.963
It's a great show.
You're wonderful in it.

00:09:24.963 --> 00:09:26.365
Hey, thanks so much
for making time for us.

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:27.533
-My pleasure.
-I really appreciate it.

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:28.800
[ Cheering and applause ]
Miles Teller, everybody.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.336
The finale of "The Offer"

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:32.337
will be released Thursday
on Paramount+

00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:35.440
